- # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`
+ # `↯/s.34.1` — `Regex.Error`

- Raised when Kaleidoscope cannot parse a regular expression literal.
- Each variant pinpoints the syntactic problem.
+ Se lanza cuando Kaleidoscope no puede analizar un literal de expresión regular. Cada variante
+ señala con precisión el problema sintáctico.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- The `r"…"` regex interpolator parses the pattern at compile time. When
- the parser cannot accept the input, it throws a `Regex.Error` carrying
- the character `index` at which the problem was detected and a `Reason`
- explaining what was expected. The constructed message is `the regular
- expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.
+ El interpolador de expresiones regulares `r"…"` analiza el patrón en tiempo de compilación.
+ Cuando el analizador no puede aceptar la entrada, lanza un `Regex.Error` que lleva el `index` del
+ carácter en el que se detectó el problema y un `Reason` que explica qué se esperaba. El mensaje
+ construido es `the regular expression could not be parsed because $reason at $index`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Code
- column  Reason
- column  Meaning
- column  Message
- column  Resolution
- row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  A capturing group was opened with `(` but never closed with `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Add the missing `)` or escape the `(` if a literal parenthesis is intended.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  An extractor pattern was used in a context that requires a capturing group to follow it, but no group was found.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Wrap the extracted portion of the pattern in `(…)`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  A repetition range `{n,m}` has `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Swap the bounds, or use `{n,}` if no upper bound is needed.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  A capturing group is nested inside a repeating group, which means it cannot be extracted unambiguously.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Either remove the capture by switching to a non-capturing group `(?:…)`, or restructure the pattern so the repetition is inside the capture rather than outside it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  A character that does not belong in a repetition range was encountered.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  Use only digits and a single comma between `{` and `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  A `)` was encountered with no corresponding `(`.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Add the missing `(`, escape the `)` if it should be literal, or remove the stray closing parenthesis.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  A repetition range was opened with `{` but never closed with `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Add the missing `}`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  The pattern was rejected by the underlying parser for a reason that does not fit any of the more specific variants.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Review the pattern around the reported index; consult the regex syntax for the construct in use.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  The pattern ends with a `\` that has nothing to escape.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Either remove the trailing backslash or escape the character that should follow it.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  A character class `[…]` contained no characters.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Add at least one character to the class, or remove the empty `[]`.
- row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  A repetition range had a maximum of zero, e.g. `{0,0}` or `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Use a maximum greater than zero, or remove the repeated subpattern entirely if it should never match.
+ column  Código
+ column  Motivo
+ column  Significado
+ column  Mensaje
+ column  Solución
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.1`  `UnclosedGroup`  Se abrió un grupo de captura con `(` pero nunca se cerró con `)`.  `[↯/s.34.1.1] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was not closed at 11`  Añade el `)` que falta o escapa el `(` si se pretende un paréntesis literal.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.2`  `ExpectedGroup`  Se usó un patrón extractor en un contexto que exige que lo siga un grupo de captura, pero no se encontró ningún grupo.  `[↯/s.34.1.2] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group was expected immediately following an extractor at 0`  Envuelve la parte extraída del patrón en `(…)`.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.3`  `BadRepetition`  Un rango de repetición `{n,m}` tiene `m < n`.  `[↯/s.34.1.3] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions is less than the minimum at 5`  Intercambia las cotas, o usa `{n,}` si no se necesita cota superior.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.4`  `Uncapturable`  Un grupo de captura está anidado dentro de un grupo que se repite, lo que significa que no puede extraerse sin ambigüedad.  `[↯/s.34.1.4] the regular expression could not be parsed because a capturing group inside a repeating group can not be extracted at 7`  Elimina la captura pasando a un grupo sin captura `(?:…)`, o reestructura el patrón para que la repetición quede dentro de la captura y no fuera.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.5`  `UnexpectedChar`  Se encontró un carácter que no corresponde a un rango de repetición.  `[↯/s.34.1.5] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range contained an unexpected character at 9`  Usa solo dígitos y una única coma entre `{` y `}`.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.6`  `NotInGroup`  Se encontró un `)` sin su `(` correspondiente.  `[↯/s.34.1.6] the regular expression could not be parsed because a closing parenthesis was found without a corresponding opening parenthesis at 4`  Añade el `(` que falta, escapa el `)` si debe ser literal, o elimina el paréntesis de cierre sobrante.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.7`  `IncompleteRepetition`  Se abrió un rango de repetición con `{` pero nunca se cerró con `}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.7] the regular expression could not be parsed because the repetition range was not closed at 8`  Añade el `}` que falta.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.8`  `InvalidPattern`  El analizador subyacente rechazó el patrón por un motivo que no encaja en ninguna de las variantes más específicas.  `[↯/s.34.1.8] the regular expression could not be parsed because the pattern was invalid at 3`  Revisa el patrón en torno al índice indicado; consulta la sintaxis de expresiones regulares de la construcción que se usa.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.9`  `UnclosedEscape`  El patrón termina con un `\` que no tiene nada que escapar.  `` [↯/s.34.1.9] the regular expression could not be parsed because nothing followed the escape character `\` at 12 ``  Elimina la barra invertida final o escapa el carácter que debería seguirla.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.10`  `EmptyCharClass`  Una clase de caracteres `[…]` no contenía ningún carácter.  `[↯/s.34.1.10] the regular expression could not be parsed because the character class is empty at 2`  Añade al menos un carácter a la clase, o elimina el `[]` vacío.
+ row  `↯/s.34.1.11`  `ZeroMaximum`  Un rango de repetición tenía un máximo de cero, por ejemplo `{0,0}` o `{0}`.  `[↯/s.34.1.11] the regular expression could not be parsed because the maximum number of repetitions must be greater than zero at 6`  Usa un máximo mayor que cero, o elimina por completo el subpatrón repetido si nunca debe coincidir.

